IaC repo for a self-hosted AI agent runtime (Hermes + Headroom) on OVHcloud VPS running NixOS + k3s.

***REMOVED******REMOVED*** Architecture snapshot

```
Local: opencode → Headroom(:8787) → minimax.io
VPS:   Caddy(host) → NodePort → k3s { Hermes Agent, Headroom proxy, Uptime Kuma, n8n, Zitadel }
```

Caddy runs as a NixOS service on the host (not k8s Ingress). It proxies to k8s services **via NodePort**. Don't use ClusterIP or k8s Ingress — Caddy does TLS termination. NodePort mappings: Hermes=30080, Uptime Kuma=30001, n8n=30002, Zitadel=30003. Headroom is ClusterIP-only (internal).

k3s is installed with `--disable traefik --disable servicelb`. Traefik conflicts with Caddy.

***REMOVED******REMOVED*** Deploy order (exact)

```
tofu apply  →  nixos-infect  →  ansible  →  nixos-rebuild  →  helmfile  →  kubectl apply
```

Use `./scripts/deploy.sh` with phase skip flags (`--skip-tofu`, `--skip-infect`, etc.). Do not skip phases or reorder.

**Pre-deploy:** create an S3-compatible object storage bucket for state first:
```bash
aws s3 mb s3://${PROJECT_NAME}-tofu-state --endpoint-url https://s3.${DATACENTER}.io.REDACTED-OVH-DOMAIN
```

**After tofu:** VPS boots Debian 12. Convert to NixOS:
```bash
ssh root@$VPS_IP 'curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elitak/nixos-infect/master/nixos-infect \
  | NIX_CHANNEL=nixos-unstable bash'
```

**NixOS:** NixOS config lives in the separate `nix-config` repo (`~/Workspace/github.com/rbelem/nix-config`). Deploy with `nixos-rebuild switch --flake path:$NIX_CONFIG_DIR#agent --target-host root@$VPS_IP`.

**Ansible secrets** are split into two playbooks: `secrets-render.yml` runs on the **workstation** (localhost, connection: local) and renders Bitwarden vault items to `.rendered/` (gitignored). `secrets-apply.yml` runs on the **VPS** and copies the pinned allowlist from `.rendered/` to the VPS. The master password never touches the VPS — bitw on the workstation uses libsecret (cached master password) or `PASSWORD` env. The VPS has no bitw binary, no `/root/.bw_master_pw`, no `/etc/agent/bw_master_pw`. Compromise of the VPS yields only rendered runtime secrets (bounded blast radius), not the master password (force multiplier).

If the workstation is unavailable, the VPS cannot self-heal secrets. Recovery: new workstation → `bitw login` → libsecret store → re-render.

**k8s manifests:** rsync to `/opt/k8s/` on VPS, then `kubectl apply -f /opt/k8s/manifests/hermes/` etc. Namespaces are managed by Ansible (`namespace_list` in `ansible/inventory/hosts.yml`).

